meta {
  name: Cost Report
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/rag/cost-report
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

docs {
  Returns today's per-operation cost breakdown for the calling team.

  This is the gateway's differentiating endpoint — it answers "which stage of
  my RAG pipeline is consuming my budget?" rather than just "which model?".

  Response example:
  ```json
  {
    "team": "product-search",
    "date": "2026-05-23",
    "total_cost_usd": 0.847,
    "by_operation": {
      "retrieval":  0.12,
      "reranking":  0.08,
      "generation": 0.58,
      "evaluation": 0.067
    }
  }
  ```

  The four named operations are always present (zero-filled if no spend).
  `unknown` appears only if non-zero spend was recorded with an unrecognised tag.

  Run `make demo` first to populate the ledger with sample data.
}
